      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0023" n="art0023">
        <head>LOCAL ODEFELLOWSHIP.</head>
        <p>LOCAL ODEFELLOWSHIP.</p>
        <p>Indepudent Order of Oddfelows (rilianchester Unity.)</p>
        <p>The quarterly district meeting was held on Saturdar, ' at the 'Navigation" Lodge, Coach and Hoises lOteir Cadishead, %%hen there were ; resent :—Prov. Grant Master G. F. Freeman (presiding), Ploy. Deputy Gran '1 T. P. Forbes, I P.P.G.M. Lot Brooks, P.q; Thomas 'Wadsworth (district treasurer), PT.° -I‘3- Frank Webster (corresponding secretary), and the P following elegates :—" Constitution " Lodge: • Peter Lester and P.G. Henry Taslor ; "William Savage Lodge : P.G. N. McQuire ; "Navigation " Lodge P.G. Joser h Grant and P.G. William BrooLs • " Olive Branch "Lodge : P.P.G.M. All an Boyle and p.G. A- Butterwor Eh ; " Prince of Wa'es "Lode : P. Brad.El,aw, P.O. A. B. Marsh end P.O. W. King ;. " Trafford " Lodge: P.G. John VE rester ; "Travellers Rest" Locge : P.G. Thomas I.`oWnes ; " Nelson " Lodge : P.G. Walter Dennt tt and V.G. Burrows ; "Haven c f Rest" Lodge ; P.G. Thon.B4- CritEhley. There Asas a fair compliment the memhers of the Oddfellow s' Cycling ell,' with P.G. Will'am King (entaint rnd A. E. Spann (secretary). Toe Grani Moter haying welcomed the delegates ,the correspond og secretary presented the accounts and auditors' iePcr'' which showed again to the funeral fend for the PI quarter of £lO7, makir g. the total wotth of the turd £3,640, (Applause). The sane were duly passed and vote - vote of thanks was accorded to the auditors P.G- Gilbert and V.G. Ashtur.—For the rosition of district' auditor there NI ere five rot-114 ations End the resulted in P.G. A. E. Marsh (" Prince of Wales Lodge) leing appointrd.—The Grand Mastfr (Bro. the- 0. F. Freeman) was appointed a trustee in place of Bro. Thomas %little, dec:vsed (of thce' " Prince of Wales" Lodge). Prov. Deputy Grand , elect Master T. P. Forbes gave the report on behalf of ther representatives of the proceedings of the Lancasl.l:o" and Adjacent Districts Conference held at Manchester," and it proved very instructive.—Bros. T. P. Fortes, T. P. Bradshaw, W. Holbrook, and A. E. Spann ner°- appointed