        <p>LANCASTIIRE .co YORKSHIRE.—This return match takes place on Saturday, July 24th, at Flixton. The result will practically decide the County Championship, The following team has been cl.osen to represebt Lancashire: J. W. G. Coombs, C. W. Smith, and H. S. Cornolley (Roebuck, Flixt on), R. Williamson, G. Drink- water, and H. Arnold (Didsbury), T. Glover, J. Grundy, and H. Harrison (Leigh Railway), A. Gleave and J. Weave (Warrington Bull's Head), T. Ellis and A. Scott (Warrington Cemetery), H. Sharpies and W. Smith (Pendleton Belmont), H. Robinson (Radcliffe Withins), T. Dutton (Bowdon), J. We sthead(Harpurhey Cemetery), G. Burnell (Unswortb), J. Blooks (Cadishrn,d Railway), P. Talbot (Sewton-le-Willows), T. B. Burgess (Winning- ton Park), J. Tootill (Kersal),aud J. Fairhurst (Chorlton Bowling Green). Rese. ;es—H. Thomason (Kuntsford), Bedworth (Warrington Bull's Head), J. E. Codling (George), J. H. Hulbert and J. Ant%is (Albion), and W. Gresty (Stretford Angel).</p>
        <p>, LANCASHIRE AND CHESHIRE AT ITEURS.</p>
        <p>At the Albion Hotel Manehekter, on Tuesday night, the thaw for the semi finale of the County Club champior ship resulte I as follows : Warrington Cen.etery v. CLorlton Bowling Grt :n Whitefield. Leigh P^alway v. Newton-k-SN Plows, atl Radcliffe Withins.</p>
        <p>Consolatioa Competitian. Setni-Cnals : STA inton Sccial v. Pendit-ti.n Woolpack, at Eccles Cross Keys. Irlann-o-th'-Height v. Sain-..0n Liberal, at Pendleton Belmont.</p>
        <p>Second Team Competitior —Semi-finals: Leigh Railaay v. Whitetield. bt Ship Irlain. Warrington Cemetery v. Radcliffe Withens at Wigan Subscription. All these matches to be playei on Saturday, July 3]. WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>Further ptorress was made in the individual merit handicap on le) lands Recreation Grouni tn Saturday afternoon. There was a big attendance, and some good bowling was witnessed. The second round was only composed of two ties. Scores :</p>
        <p>SECOND ROUND. Iltinacr R. Ailesden had a walk-over. THI:ID ROUND.</p>
