        <p>'Ma following is a list, arranged alphabetically, of the candidates who have b..en successful in passg the exemination for junior acholarships of the value of £3 per annum, together with free tuition at the Secondary School arid thenecessary books for one year from Ict Atteust, 1909, viz :—Harold Bates, Elsie Colley, James R. Dewar, Arthur Greenough,Jessie Groake,Doris Joller, Nfargaret Kilgallon, Nellie Littlewood, Hilda Newell John o.kes, Direst H. Parsons Edgar l' Perk., Limy Wgby, Margaret Side%ll, Hilda Small- wood, John A. Thompson, Arthur Ti lbr, Lily Wainwright, Walter Wellington, Midi- V. Wilc,rck. The following is a list, arranged alphabetically, of the candidates who l'ave been awarded "Honorary Scholarships" on the result of the recent examination for Junior Scholarship. The tcholar.hips will entitle the holders so free tuition at the Secondary School but the necpsEary texts and exercise taroks will not E 3 provide, viz. :-17abel Harding, Mice Jarman, Doris Mary Locker, Hilda M. L. W.-s'cott, Jessle Wilkinson</p>
