      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0065" n="art0065">
        <head>Mother's Many</head>
        <p>A Mother's Many</p>
        <p>Woes</p>
        <p>cured by the Rich Red Blood that she found in Dr. William's Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>The trials and ills that so often weigh down woman following following the precious gift of motherhood are clearly indicated by Mrs. Myers, of 27,•Crawford-street. Leeds. Herself, the m tiler of . four bonny children. the delight of mothei ing hem was at one time dimmed by protracted sufferings, though she tells now with evident gratitude how those ills were cure&amp; by Pr. Williams' Pink Pills. "After I married and had a family," raid Mrg• Myers," it was a sruggle soire days to keep going' for my -head and back troubled me a lot and I felt downi ight ill and depressede "About two years ago I ate scarcely two mouthful: r 1 of food a day, for meal caused flatulence • and bilious sickness. Sink- ing sensations used t? creep over me and I felt as though I going to to die. I really too ill to after the children anu at times .could not see a yard before me. "All may bones ached, and my joints were so, full of pain that I had- difficulty in bending al limbs. "A doctor said ant' I was breaking up frora the want of blood awl he ordered me to remain in bed. I took medicine for quite a long time. "I was really too ill to but grew .thinner and look after my children." th inner ;my nerves became shattered and Neuralgia t-oubled me. " At length no one thought that I was long for this world. I wasted to a skeleton and had not s •englit enough to raise my hands to my head. "However one afternoon a nighbour who bad liqd siniilar troubles begged me to try a course of pr. Williams' Pink Pills. ' Listen to the ads' 'ea of 3 woman who has had similar troubles and knows how to cure them,' she said, so I sent for a supply of the Pills.</p>
        <p>"When I had taken the contents of three boxes I felt almost well enough to leave my bed, 31Y husband urged me to persevere, and are; I bad take,' a few more boxes my appetite improved daily and could take nomishment without pain or diseon- 'ort. "I became stronger and stronger and one dal stnprised my family by dressing myself and walking downstairs. My back was still very weak, but I mad"' the same effort daily-, and before long I wrs getting about my household duties again as we!! as ever. WY, cure was soon completed. I improved in weight an" colour and am more robust than ever—quite like a new woman."</p>
        <p>ESTABLISHED 60 YEARS (in Warrington). Tel. No. I_-23.</p>
        <p>The many woes that ac!:?ompany motherhood orc: often due to Weak, Impure Blood. Dr. Williams Pink Pills supply the New, Good Blood that makes Women well. Thus they have cured Antonia, Debility, the After-Effects of Influenza, Nervous Pis- ordefs, Indigestion. Rheumatism, Sciatica, Neuralgia; St. 'Vitus' Dance, and Paralysis ; also the aches fm" ills of women. Obtainable of dealers, or from Pr' Williams' Medicine Co., 46, Bolbofn Viaduct, Londoa, post free, 2s. 9d. for one box, or 13s. 9d. for six. ,</p>
