      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>FLYING THE ENGLISH CHANNEL.</head>
        <p>FLYING THE ENGLISH CHANNEL.</p>
        <p>, Mr. Hubert Latham intends to be the first man to fly across the English Channel, and Ind for an unfavourable breeze he would have made the attempt on Saturday. Mr. Latham, 11110 i$ twenty-six years of age, is a Parisian by birth, but his father 's a Lancashire man, and he himself was ai Oxford, where he gained a taste for English sports. - In 1905 he accompanied M. Jacques Faure in the record balloon trip from the Crystal Palace to the Eates ai Paris In six hours, and the same year he drove at Monte Carlo a motor-boat devised YM. Levavassour, the maker of the motor of his present monoplane, Antoinette the Fourth. .._•11 our photograph Mr. Latham (on the left) is accompanied by Mr. Seymour, a monoplant "4ventor, who is also said to be contemplating a Channel flight.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0068" n="art0068">
        <p>CROWD. toutrilre Oval will know Craig no more. His to ~ing face and ready repartee were familiar it au followers of County Cricket, and there trill° doubt that the Surrey poet and -Hs ad._cilet rhymes will be missed by his many 6:44.lrers. He was cheered in his lust illness hi a Message from the Prince of Wales, who OPed that his friends might soon welcome 4131 back tythe Oval.</p>
        <p>THE CROWN PRINCESS OF GERMANY.</p>
        <p>t 4 The Crown Prince and Princess of Germany are looking forward to thcir coming visit 2. England with the keenest possible interest. This will be the Crown Princess's first ov!sit to our shores, and in Her Royal Highness, English society will make the acquaintance an exceedingly charming young lady. The Crown Prince and Princess enjoy the .13utation of being more in love with each other than any other Royal couple in the world, ,eleir home life being an ideally happy One. Oar photograph shows the Crown Princess a§ kolpncl pf her Cavalry regiment, •</p>
        <p>THE PROBATION JUDGE. JUDGE JEFF. POLLARD OF ST. LOUIS.</p>
        <p>Judge Jeff. Pollard, of St. Louis, the United States delegate to the International Congress on Alcoholism which meat in London on Monday, is the founder of the probation system of dealing with drunkards. Every convicted "drunk" has ,to chose between going to prison. .or signing the pledge:and after a nine years' trial Judge Pollard can claim that 95 per cent. of these who took the oath have kept it.</p>
