        <p>Appleton.</p>
        <p>POWL STEALING--At the Daresbury Petty Sessions, nLo Tuesday, Frank Millington. a man of no settled 7"°d,e, was charged with stealing on June 16th two ;./).7,Lar of the value of 55., the property of Joseph farmer, Appleton. He pleaded not guilty.—The ridence showed that prisoner did some work at the On June 16th the fowLs were missed and prisoner ias seen going along the footpath about 100 yards ruin the farm, with something an ter his arm. Later t:e Sold two fowls to Mr. Hormel!, licensee of the Cattle iglarket Inn, NVarrington, stating that he kept a farm at Vretten, rind as it was over-run with fowls he was Illitg them c,ff. When seen by Detective Clough prisoner said he had bought the fowls from a Jew.— -,ctine-Sergeant Thtstock said when charged the gefecdant said "When anything is vt arrg it's always 114e."—Prisr ner told the Bench he bougnt the fowls r°4ll a man from Manchester.—There was a preohtus t°o‘iction for fowl stealing agairst prisoner, and he Ilos sent to gaol for oce month.</p>
