      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0105" n="art0105">
        <head>LOCAL DRUIDISM.</head>
        <p>LOCAL DRUIDISM.</p>
        <p>Initiation of New Honorary Members.</p>
        <p>Notwithstanding the outdoor allurements of a delightful July evening, memters of the Waerington District of the Ancient Order of Druids mustered in rcng force at a meeting and sine kirg concert held at the Patten Ants Hotel on Motelay evening for then joint purposes of initiating three honorary int mbers— Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart., Mr. Robert P.erpoinr, and Councillor Fulton-Smith—and of distrituting U e prizes gained in the recent bowling handicap. The gathering was honoured with the presence of several members of the Board of Management of the Order and the attend- ance of local Druids was thoroughly represer tat ive. Grandn.aster George Blackburn, of Leeds, presided, and was supported by Vice-Grad 'Waster E. Morgan Jones (os.v estry) Past Grand Master H. Atwater (Newcastle-on-Tyne), Bros. Copping (Darlington), Gage (Brist:rl), Makinson (Chorle)r, Stanley (Newcastle), Hawley (Sheffield), McLardy (Glasgow), and J. W. Shaw, Grand Secretary (Man- chester). Among.t the local brethren present were : Bros. George D.T., E. Allen, D.C.S , R. Pooley.P.D.G.M., J.Jackson, P.D.G.M., D. Houghte n, P.G.M., S.Cald well, P.D.G.M. Rev. J. R• Jones' Dr. Murray, Bros. J. B. Aitken, and W. Daties (Penketh), Sankey (trustee). The new honorary members were presented by Bro. Allen, D.C.S., and the initiation ceremony was impressively per formed by Grand Master G. Blackburn, assisted by Vice Grand Master E. Morgan Jones. • Sir Gilbert GREENALL then distribrued the pr'zes as follows :—Sir Gilbert Gre enall's Cerallerge Cup, T. Kerfoot cf Croft ' • 2, J. Hardman ; 3. W. Goulden ; 4, R. Ihsworth, 4, D. Famekerly ; 6, E. Allen; 7, J. Lloyd ; 8, E. Dumbell ' • 9, W. itilby, jln.; 10, J. Bowyer ; 11, J. Ball ; 12, 'l'. Owen ; 13, G. Ashlt y ; 14. H. Bowyer ; 15, W. Green; 16, Ellis Maines ; 17, J. Mickey ; 18, J. W. Starkey; 19, Peter Johnson; 20, James Hardman ; 21, W. Beresford ; 22, J. Dickenson ; 23, R. Mai es ; 24, It. E. Pooler. Bro. Hall, Secretary of the gowlirg Committe?, was presented with an t.mbres with silver tacd suitably inscribed. _ _ _</p>
      </div>
