      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0108" n="art0108">
        <head>D. FRAWLEY</head>
        <p>D. FRAWLEY</p>
        <p>A big, speedy wing or 'centre three- quarter, who scored a fine try in the seemd match at Wartington. He is 24 years ...old, 51t. 10in, tall, and 11 stones 10 lbs. in weight.</p>
        <p>[TO liiE .EDITOII "EXAMINER."]</p>
        <p>. Sir' —Alloiv me in the first place to compliment you on the vast improvement of your paper, especially on your souvenir number. I consider it is now an ide4l we kly newspaper and by far the Lest wet kly in this district.</p>
        <p>Can you also find me space in your issue to con- gratulate the committee of the Warrington Rugby Club for allowing the enterprise in :ecuring such well-knoN% n players as o‘‘lalley and Frawley, of the last Australian team, and if the rumour is correct several other gr od players ale likely to be booted before the playing teason is opened lam sure sach a step as this is an omen of what the new blood in the committee wiil do, and I have no doubt that the money exp Ended on players of'this class will be recovered by a vastly increased membetship. I also noti, -1. from your nev‘spaper that the accommodatiln for spectators is to bq increased, and I trnst the commit' - 3 will give this question all their attention, for I censider, sit tr,ted as we are, the Northern Union Committee could do worse than to play a Caunty Match, or a NorthetA Uunion Cup Semi- final on this ground. Yours tru!y, A PROSPECTIVE MEMBER.</p>
        <p>Devon. .-C.cy ornwall</p>
