        <p>BOWLING. (Continued from Page 3.) Warrington and District Association. The final of the above competition will take place to-day on the bowling green attached to the Matteis' Brothers' Recreation ground and will commence at 2 o'clock a hen the remlin- ing 32 plalers will compete rar tha 16 prizes. Some very keen games are expected as some of the most notable blwlers in3luling several Lancashire County men will take part. The draw will be held just before the match in the presence of the competitors.</p>
        <p>INDIVIDUAL MERIT COMPETITION. , R.A.O B. MAIN.</p>
        <p>The annuli handiclp miin in connectian with the four local-lodges of the R.A.0.8. in Warrington and Stocktcn Heath was held at the Dog and Dart, Grappenhall, on Thursday afternoon. The games throughont proved very enjoyable, and the hmdicapping of the committee was very satisfactory. Results :</p>
