      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-07-17_WidnesExaminer_art0131" n="art0131">
        <head>WIRRAL AGRICULTURAL SHOW.</head>
        <p>WIRRAL AGRICULTURAL SHOW.</p>
        <p>This annual thres days show opened at Bebingt" rs Tuesday, and was continued over Wednesday and Too—j bay in fine weather. Record crowds have attended, 5q tha show has in every respect being a huge success• the excellence of its chietexhibits and of its marvig`tv meat the show continues to deserve description as, it county show in miniature. As Ches.hire has not A county show of its own it is as well that societleo intended to supply the needs of limited areas sh°ll ; have ambition enough for special effort, and thlli attract something of the best that the agriculturisis u°,s the country can produce. The Wirral Society tip„ci care to maintain a fair proportion of open classes, one never fails to find in the rings, animals which 11° won national repu'ations as prize-winners.</p>
        <p>Mr. Edward Porritt. At the meeting of the Corporation of Harvar University on Monday, Mr. Edward Porritt, i°e Hartford, was re-appointed special lecturer in tltt department of Government and History. ..• Mr. Prn.l.",c during the last college year took the place of Profes% Macvane, and lectured on modern English histr. 4i His lectures at Harvard next year will be on Eng'4; party history and on responsible government in "(r. British Colonies. - As during the past college year Porritt will spend part of each week at Cambridge 314 part at his home in Hartford. Mr. and Mrs. are leaving the city July 14th for a visit to Englanui, returning to Hartford on August 30th.—The Hartferci "Daily Courant," Conn., U.S.A., July 2nd. Co-operative Quarterly Meeting., rif Mr. T. Wadsworth presided over the ciaarte. meeting of the Warrington Co-operative Sociekvr which was held on Monday evening in Bold-street. Wesleyan schoolroom. The following members ° the Committee were present :—Messrs. W. 13,ibbil: J. W. Bouchier, 'N. Cook, W. Haigh, B. Hall, 1'; Hibbert, G. T. Rushton, F. Timperley, E. Ellgl''-r) and J. Edge; also Mr. W: Atkinson (general rnanag,ee'er and Mr. J. Jarman (secretary):—The Cora4s reported that the sales for the quarter were 15..0,.1 14s. 1161. for ,14 weeks. as against £51,98525. .1". the corresponding 14 weeks of last pear: or an incl.° of £4,760 us. 6d. The profits realised enabled theil; to recommend a dividend of 3s. 2d. in the 14 members' purchases, one per cent. to the Educatl Fund, and a small balance to the diviti,e,,lC; equalization fund. During the quarter 281 eft members had joined and 80 lapsed or of the district, leaving the net membershiP tit 9,371. The Council suggested that £2OO be rAhe aside toward the forthcoming celebration of t'tee, Societys jubilee.—The President said the Cortlibat were agreeably surprised during the past quarter 'tile the sales had kept up so well. .As they knell', prices of provisions and other materials had u 1 ,1a considerably during the last quarter, and this caused them great anxiety. The building in SarrbeY street would be proceeded with 'more rapidly. l tii had had to wait for material, but he was hopefuo3-• before next quarterly meeting it would be almost thief • pleted. With regard .to the children's gala day, had been successful in making an arrangement a ja, the Football Club for the use of their grounA August, and they expected to have 3,500 chil'ter a. present..- The report and balance sheet were adq era The three retiring members of the committee vcaod Messrs. W. Haigh, E. England, and B. Farra,c, they were again nominated together with Howliston. On a ballot being taken, the voting l; as follows :—Mr. W: Haigh, 91; Mr.. E. England,iri4 Mr. B. Farrar, 68 ; Mr. T. Howliston, 56. There members were, therefore, re-elected. 0014 Warrington.—Printed and published by JOHN zu ioef' lc Co., (Warrington) Ltd., !at The General Printing 'Norio, Be.wsey-street,i also published by them at , the same place, 0n..,7005:. at The Examiner Offices, Victoria-roae, ctre 32, George-street, Sr. HELM: 3, Market EARLESTOWN; Church-street Itrticomr, July 17t-</p>
